cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use HyperHex in research or teaching, please cite this software and
  identify the exact commit or release used. Citation is requested, not an
  additional software-license condition.
type: software
title: "HyperHex: Urban Low-Altitude Drone Corridor Research Simulator"
authors:
  - family-names: Yegireddi
    given-names: Naresh
repository-code: "https://github.com/nashyegi/hyperhex"
url: "https://hyperhex.dev"
abstract: >-
  HyperHex is a research prototype for exploring urban low-altitude drone
  corridors using H3 geographic cells, altitude layers, and discrete time slots.
  It combines interval-based reservations, safe-interval path planning, and an
  interactive 3D workbench for synthetic controller comparisons and route-repair
  experiments. It is not an operational drone-control system.
keywords:
  - urban low-altitude drone corridors
  - geospatial indexing
  - H3
  - safe interval path planning
  - four-dimensional reservations
  - research simulation
license: AGPL-3.0-only
